<title>MALAYSIA: MBf opens 1.2 rgt lower on requotation.</title>
<headline>MBf opens 1.2 rgt lower on requotation.</headline>
<dateline>KUALA LUMPUR 1997-06-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>MBf Capital Bhd, whose application for a merger with Suria Capital was rejected by the central bank recently, opened 1.2 ringgit lower after 18-days in suspension.</p>
<p>The share opened at 4.0 ringgit and recovered to 4.3 ringgit a few minutes later.</p>
<p>The share was suspended from trading on June 7 after MBf applied to Bank Negara for the takeover.</p>
<p>&quot;The share had a good run before the suspension on hopes that the merger will go through,&quot; said a dealer with the international division of a retail-based brokerage.</p>
<p>He said the market was disappointed with the rejection of MBf's merger plan.</p>
<p>-- Kuala Lumpur newsroom (603-201 4813)</p>
